---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { getSiteData } from '../lib/baserow';

const data = await getSiteData();
const s = data.settings;
const contactEmail = s.contactEmail || 'info@rootedcommons.uk';
---
<BaseLayout settings={s} pages={data.pages} title="Privacy notice" description="How Roots to Fruits CIC uses and protects personal information through Rooted Commons.">
  <main class="legal-page">
    <article class="legal-content">
      <p class="eyebrow">Rooted Commons</p>
      <h1>Privacy notice</h1>
      <p class="small-print">Last updated: 5 August 2026</p>

      <p>This notice explains how Roots to Fruits CIC uses personal information through Rooted Commons.</p>

      <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
      <p><strong>Roots to Fruits CIC is the data controller for Rooted Commons.</strong></p>
      <p>Company number: 14699477<br />
      Registered office: 95 St. Michael's Road, Aldershot, GU12 4JJ<br />
      Email: <a href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`}>{contactEmail}</a></p>

      <h2>2. Information we collect</h2>
      <p>Depending on how you use Rooted Commons, we may collect your name, email address, phone number, membership status and reference, regular commitment, collection preferences, optional-news preference, Member Credit, order history, payment and refund records, communications with us, and technical information needed to operate and secure the website.</p>
      <p>We do not ask you to enter full payment-card details into our website. Where online payment is offered, the payment provider processes the payment details needed to complete it.</p>

      <h2>3. How and why we use your information</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Membership and orders:</strong> to create and administer your membership, provide secure account access, process orders, arrange collection and maintain Member Credit. This is necessary to provide the membership and ordering service you request.</li>
        <li><strong>Payments and records:</strong> to record payments, refunds and accounting entries and meet our tax, company and financial-record obligations. We rely on our agreement with you and our legal obligations.</li>
        <li><strong>Administration and security:</strong> to prevent unauthorised use, investigate faults, maintain the service and protect our systems. We rely on our legitimate interests in operating Rooted Commons reliably and securely.</li>
        <li><strong>Essential communications:</strong> to send the secure links and service messages needed to operate your membership, including information about your account, orders and collections.</li>
        <li><strong>Optional news:</strong> if you choose to receive Rooted Commons news and updates, we use your consent for that optional content. You can withdraw your consent at any time without affecting your membership.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>4. Information we need from you</h2>
      <p>We need your name, email address and the other information required to administer your membership and orders. Without this information we may not be able to create or operate your membership or fulfil an order. Information used only for optional communications is voluntary.</p>

      <h2>5. Who we share information with</h2>
      <p>We use trusted service providers to help us operate Rooted Commons, including website hosting and security providers, database and account-management services, email providers, accounting services and, where applicable, payment processors. They receive only the information reasonably necessary for the service they provide.</p>
      <p>We may also share the minimum information necessary with staff, volunteers, producers and collection-point partners where they need it to prepare or hand over an order. We may disclose information where required by law or where necessary to establish, exercise or defend legal claims.</p>

      <h2>6. International transfers</h2>
      <p>Some service providers may process personal information outside the United Kingdom. Where personal information is transferred internationally, we use providers and safeguards intended to meet UK data-protection requirements, such as UK adequacy regulations or approved contractual safeguards where required.</p>

      <h2>7. How long we keep information</h2>
      <p>We keep membership and account information while your membership is active and for as long afterwards as reasonably necessary to close the account and deal with queries. Financial and transaction records that we need for tax, accounting or legal purposes may be retained for up to seven years.</p>
      <p>Expired authentication tokens are deleted, replaced or cease to be usable when they are no longer needed. Routine enquiries and other information are deleted or anonymised when we no longer reasonably need them for the purpose for which they were collected, unless we need to retain them to resolve a dispute or meet a legal requirement.</p>

      <h2>8. Website storage and cookies</h2>
      <p>The website uses local storage or similar technology on your device to remember things such as your basket, collection preferences and secure member access. This storage is used to provide the functions you request.</p>
      <p>We do not currently use non-essential advertising cookies. If we introduce non-essential analytics or marketing technologies, we will provide appropriate information and choices before using them where consent is required.</p>

      <h2>9. Your rights</h2>
      <p>Depending on the circumstances, you may have the right to ask for a copy of your personal information, correct inaccurate information, request deletion or restriction, object to certain uses, and receive information you provided in a portable format. You have the right to object to direct marketing. Where processing is based on consent, you can withdraw that consent at any time without affecting earlier lawful processing.</p>
      <p>To exercise a right or ask a privacy question, email <a href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`}>{contactEmail}</a>. We may need to confirm your identity before acting on a request.</p>

      <h2>10. Complaints</h2>
      <p>Please contact us first so we can try to resolve your concern. You also have the right to complain to the Information Commissioner's Office (ICO), the UK supervisory authority for data protection.</p>

      <h2>11. Changes to this notice</h2>
      <p>We may update this notice when Rooted Commons or our legal obligations change. The latest version will be published here with its revision date.</p>
    </article>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
